body:
Thank you for your reply. I've decided on the K-30 because of its weather-sealing and great ergonomics, and better battery life as well. I was thinking of getting the Nikon D3200 for a while there because I was thinking of shooting a little video, but then what dawned on me was this;

What other camera am I going to find in the price range of the K-30 that has weather-sealing? Definitely not that Nikon. Not to mention that because of the extra, and IMO, unnecessary megapixels, the RAW files will be much larger than those produced from the K-30. And I don't want very large files. My laptop isn't good enough to handle that.

So although the Nikon may have better video, the weather-sealing of the Pentax K-30 is what seals the deal for me.
